var coreChangelogMarkdown = map[string]string{
	"en-US": "## [0.1.0] - 2026-11-21\n\nThe first official AlonaBot release.\n\n### Added\n\n- Core and the `v0.1.0` Go SDK for independently installed plugins, adapters and agents.\n- Five platform archives: linux/amd64, linux/arm64, windows/amd64, darwin/amd64 and darwin/arm64. Windows uses ZIP; other targets use tar.gz. Standard builds use `CGO_ENABLED=0`.\n- An integrated Core + WebUI + Agent image, `ghcr.io/alonabot/alonabot:0.1.0`, with Docker Compose. WebUI is enabled on first start; configure a Provider and model before enabling Agent. Compose uses UID 10001, init, a persistent `/data` volume and a loopback port binding.\n- Separately installable Telegram and OneBot 11 adapters and the help plugin. All five official components use AGPL-3.0-only and publish signed releases; `components.lock.json` pins their versions. Image bundles verify and preserve the published component assets.\n- Component updates that retain source/publisher bindings and pin settings, and rollback into a new generation with a database copy. Installer uninstall removes services and programs while retaining data; ordinary component uninstall retains generations, data and source bindings for reinstallation from the same source.\n\n### Changed\n\n- On 2026-11-21, with maintainer approval, the five v0.1.0 archives were **repackaged in place as Core-only distributions**, containing the Core executable, `LICENSE` and `source.json`. The original Core binaries and tag are preserved; Compose images remain integrated. Existing installed components are retained. **Previous archive digests are obsolete: download the new archives and verify their new GitHub Release API asset digests.** See [PR #292](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/pull/292).\n- Release attachments contain only the five platform archives; GitHub provides source archives automatically. Download `deploy/install.sh` from `main` and `docker-compose.yml` from the version tag. The installer verifies official downloads against GitHub Release API asset digests. See [PR #291](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/pull/291).\n\n### Install and upgrade\n\nFollow the [deployment guide](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/af4f68550dcef191d5bc9a5e345b48510196ae23/docs/deployment.md). Native archives and the installer provide Core; install WebUI, Agent and adapters as needed. Compose preinstalls WebUI and Agent. For v0.1.0, claim the one-time administration token as prompted at startup; WebUI is available at `http://127.0.0.1:7650` after installation and activation. Use an SSH tunnel or HTTPS reverse proxy for remote management.\n\nBefore upgrading from a development build, stop Core and all components and back up the complete data directory, programs, packages, deployment configuration and external component data: component IDs, state layouts and initial migrations changed during development. Preserve the same volume when recreating containers. Follow [backup and recovery](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/af4f68550dcef191d5bc9a5e345b48510196ae23/docs/deployment.md#备份与恢复) for upgrade, rollback and full restoration.\n\n### Known limitations\n\n- OneBot 11 receives events; sending returns `UNSUPPORTED`. The welcome and rss plugins and the Telegram follow-up features listed in the [release agreement at that time](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/f0382910/spec/CONTRACTS-v0.1.md#152-发行包官方整合包与预装组件) remain planned.\n- Native components execute trusted local code. Library components share the Core process: an unhandled panic ends it, and a timed-out goroutine cannot be forcibly stopped.\n- Components declaring `prepare_effects=external` require explicit maintenance, backup permission and component-specific recovery for external effects.\n- The scratch image includes CA certificates. MCP stdio tools requiring shell, Node or Python need a custom image containing those runtimes.\n\n### Recorded verification\n\nHistorical acceptance covers the integrated candidate before repository extraction: darwin/arm64 ran natively, darwin/amd64 under Rosetta, linux/amd64 in an x86_64 VM and linux/arm64 in Docker on an ARM host. Native Intel Mac and ARM Linux VM/physical-host execution were not run. Windows cross-compilation and static checks passed; runtime and CGO checks were deferred with maintainer approval on 2026-11-20. Business checks used a local Telegram Bot API and synthetic Provider; final-candidate live Telegram and paid LLM credentials were not exercised. Detailed results, original failures and deferred checks remain in the [historical acceptance record](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/d8b9678931013b6d46a044dbdbb0db9182262065/spec/TEST-MATRIX.md). Checks for extracted components are recorded in their integration PR.\n\n### Resource results and dependencies\n\nThe maintainer accepted current overhead and stopped further resource measurements, load tests and optimization. Historical 24/10/16 MiB comparisons remain FAIL; new four-workload and NoneBot2 comparison runs were cancelled. Complete figures and conditions remain in the [original measurements](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/d8b9678931013b6d46a044dbdbb0db9182262065/docs/benchmarks.md).\n\nThose measurements used `github.com/AlonaBot/gorm v1.31.3-0.20261120022453-34b98340007d`; v0.1.0 uses upstream `gorm.io/gorm v1.31.2`. Binary size and runtime memory may increase after restoring upstream. Builds use Go 1.27.1 and Node 26.5.1 with locked npm dependencies; Linux ARM acceptance used Go 1.27.3.\n\n[0.1.0]: https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/releases/tag/v0.1.0\n\n## [0.1.1] - 2026-11-21\n\n### Added\n\n- Add `Context.ReadNodes` to read standard message nodes from reply and forwarded-message handles, with media grants for the calling session. Typed node queries in OneBot 11 v0.1.1 require this Core version.\n- Add portable Markdown message segments for Adapter-specific rendering, with explicit `PlainText()` conversion.\n- Add management APIs for component and Core changelogs.\n\n### Changed\n\n- Pin official OneBot 11 and WebUI components to v0.1.1; help, Agent and Telegram remain at v0.1.0. WebUI v0.1.1 adds store search, sorting, role counts, nine-card pagination and submission checks. Submission opens a GitHub Issue template in the browser.\n- Persist the management token in `admin_token` with mode `0600`; startup and token initialization/reset report its file path. Local WebUI supports token claim and confirmation, and management commands read credentials from the selected data directory.\n- `alonabot init` creates plugin and agent examples that reply with `Hello AlonaBot` directly; add i18n files when needed. Generated Go files and `plugin.yaml` contain no comments. See [PR #295](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/pull/295).\n- Provide English and Simplified Chinese READMEs with language links, documentation homepages and a shared Views badge; move brand images to `docs/assets`.\n- Public Releases continue to contain only five platform-specific Core archives, each containing Core, `LICENSE` and `source.json`. Compose uses `ghcr.io/alonabot/alonabot:0.1.1` with WebUI and Agent included. Existing release assets and tags are retained.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Preserve media authorization and mount paths when serving media URLs, and register queried-node media for the calling session.\n- Return published Core changelogs in English or Simplified Chinese according to `Accept-Language`, with English fallback, so the update view can display versioned release notes. Exclude unreleased changes from the API. See [PR #295](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/pull/295).\n\n### Upgrade and compatibility\n\nStop Core normally and back up the complete data directory before upgrading. Replace the executable or update the pinned Compose image, then start with the same data directory. Installation records, source bindings, component generations and Adapter instance configuration are retained. Normal component uninstall retains data and source bindings for reinstallation from the same source.\n\nManagement commands use `--data-dir` in place of `--token-file` or `ALONABOT_ADMIN_TOKEN`; use SSH or `docker exec` for a remote Core. If an older login removed `admin_token`, stop Core and run `alonabot admin-token reset --data-dir <data_dir>` to restore local CLI access. Reset revokes existing management sessions.\n\nOneBot 11 v0.1.1 can start on Core v0.1.0. Node queries use the new Core service and return `Core service not found` on the older version; upgrade Core to use them. Official components retain their independent signed-release installation flow. Help remains at v0.1.0.\n\nThis version was cross-built for all five targets and passed archive checks on darwin/arm64. CLI and HTTP management paths passed installation, activation, uninstall and same-source reinstallation of public signed components. Public OneBot 11 v0.1.1 and help v0.1.0 returned real `/help` replies in an authorized QQ test group before and after Core restart, retaining installation records, Active generations and instance configuration.\n\nOther actual platform coverage and approved deferrals carry forward from the [v0.1.0 release record](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/main/changelog/v0.1.0/en.md). Windows execution and CGO retain their approved deferrals.\n\n[0.1.1]: https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/releases/tag/v0.1.1\n\n",
	"zh-CN": "## [0.1.0] - 2026-11-21\n\nAlonaBot 首个正式版本。\n\n<a id=\"发行内容\"></a>\n\n### Added\n\n- 提供 Core 与 `v0.1.0` Go SDK，支持独立安装的插件、Adapter 和 Agent。\n- 提供 linux/amd64、linux/arm64、windows/amd64、darwin/amd64、darwin/arm64 五平台归档。Windows 使用 ZIP，其余使用 tar.gz；普通发行物为 `CGO_ENABLED=0`。\n- 提供 Core + WebUI + Agent 整合镜像 `ghcr.io/alonabot/alonabot:0.1.0` 与 Docker Compose。首次启动启用 WebUI；Agent 配置 Provider 与模型后由管理员启用。Compose 使用 UID 10001、init、持久化 `/data` 卷和 loopback 端口绑定。\n- 提供按需安装的 Telegram、OneBot 11 Adapter 与 help 插件。五个官方组件均采用 AGPL-3.0-only 并独立发布签名发行物，`components.lock.json` 固定组件版本；镜像整合包验签后原样收录已发布组件资产。\n- 组件更新保留来源、发布者绑定与 pin 设置，回退建立独立新代次及数据库副本。安装器卸载服务和程序时保留数据；组件普通卸载保留代次、数据与来源，允许同来源重装。\n\n### Changed\n\n- 2026-11-21 经维护者批准，v0.1.0 五个平台归档**原地重包为纯 Core**，仅包含 Core 可执行文件、`LICENSE` 和 `source.json`。原 Core 二进制与 tag 保留，Compose 镜像继续提供整合包，数据目录中已有组件继续保留。**旧归档摘要失效，请重新下载并按 GitHub Release API 的新资产摘要校验。**见 [PR #292](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/pull/292)。\n- Release 附件仅保留五个平台归档，源码压缩包由 GitHub 自动提供。`deploy/install.sh` 从 `main` 下载，`docker-compose.yml` 从版本 tag 下载；安装器使用 GitHub Release API 的资产摘要校验官方下载。见 [PR #291](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/pull/291)。\n\n### 安装与升级\n\n按[安装与部署](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/af4f68550dcef191d5bc9a5e345b48510196ae23/docs/deployment.md)操作。原生归档与安装器提供 Core，WebUI、Agent 和 Adapter 按需安装；Compose 预装 WebUI 与 Agent。v0.1.0 按启动提示领取一次性管理 token，WebUI 安装并启用后可在 `http://127.0.0.1:7650` 登录。远程管理使用 SSH 隧道或 HTTPS 反向代理。\n\n从开发版本升级前，停止 Core 与全部组件，备份完整数据目录、程序、安装包、部署配置和外部组件数据；开发期间组件 ID、状态结构和初始迁移已有调整。重建容器时保留同一数据卷。升级、回退与整套恢复按[备份与恢复](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/af4f68550dcef191d5bc9a5e345b48510196ae23/docs/deployment.md#备份与恢复)操作。\n\n### 已知限制\n\n- OneBot 11 支持接收事件，发送返回 `UNSUPPORTED`；welcome、rss 插件与 [当时发行约定](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/f0382910/spec/CONTRACTS-v0.1.md#152-发行包官方整合包与预装组件) 列出的 Telegram 后续功能留待后续发行。\n- Native 组件是管理员信任的本机代码。库模式共享 Core 进程，未捕获 panic 会结束进程，停止超时无法强制结束 goroutine。\n- 声明 `prepare_effects=external` 的组件需显式维护、备份许可及针对外部副作用的组件专用恢复流程。\n- scratch 镜像包含 CA 证书；需要 shell、Node 或 Python 的 MCP stdio 工具应自行构建含相应运行时的镜像。\n\n### 验证记录\n\n历史验收对应拆仓前整合候选：darwin/arm64 原生运行，darwin/amd64 使用 Rosetta，linux/amd64 使用 x86_64 VM，linux/arm64 使用 ARM 宿主上的 Docker；Intel Mac 原生与 ARM Linux VM/物理机未运行。Windows 交叉构建与静态检查通过，实际运行和 CGO 于 2026-11-20 经维护者批准延期。业务联验使用本地 Telegram Bot API 与合成 Provider，最终候选的真实 Telegram 与付费 LLM 凭据未运行。逐项结果、原始失败和延期项见[历史验收记录](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/d8b9678931013b6d46a044dbdbb0db9182262065/spec/TEST-MATRIX.md)；组件拆仓后的定向检查随对应整合 PR 记录。\n\n### 资源与依赖\n\n维护者已接受现有开销并停止新增资源测量、压测和优化。历史 24/10/16 MiB 比较保留 FAIL，原四负载及 NoneBot2 对照取消新增运行；完整数字和条件见[资源实测记录](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/d8b9678931013b6d46a044dbdbb0db9182262065/docs/benchmarks.md)。\n\n历史测量使用 `github.com/AlonaBot/gorm v1.31.3-0.20261120022453-34b98340007d`；v0.1.0 使用上游 `gorm.io/gorm v1.31.2`，恢复上游后的产物体积与运行内存可能增加。构建使用 Go 1.27.1、Node 26.5.1 与锁定的 npm 依赖，Linux ARM 平台验收使用 Go 1.27.3。\n\n[0.1.0]: https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/releases/tag/v0.1.0\n\n## [0.1.1] - 2026-11-21\n\n### Added\n\n- 增加 `Context.ReadNodes`，按引用或合并转发的句柄读取标准消息节点，并为返回的媒体签发当前会话的读取权限。OneBot 11 v0.1.1 的类型化节点查询需要本版 Core。\n- 增加通用 Markdown 消息片段，支持由 Adapter 映射到平台格式；`PlainText()` 可显式转换为纯文本。\n- 提供组件与 Core 更新日志的管理 API。\n\n### Changed\n\n- 官方组件锁定 OneBot 11 v0.1.1 与 WebUI v0.1.1，help、Agent 和 Telegram 保持 v0.1.0。WebUI v0.1.1 提供商店搜索、排序、角色计数、九卡片分页和收录检查；收录申请通过浏览器打开 GitHub Issue 模板。\n- 管理 token 以 `0600` 权限持久保存在 `admin_token`，启动与凭据初始化、重置只输出文件路径。本机 WebUI 支持领取和确认凭据，管理 CLI 自动读取所选数据目录中的凭据。\n- `alonabot init` 创建的 plugin/agent 示例直接回复 `Hello AlonaBot`，按需自行添加 i18n 文件；各角色生成的 Go 文件和 `plugin.yaml` 均无注释。见 [PR #295](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/pull/295)。\n- 提供中英文 README、语言互切、各语言文档首页与共享 Views 徽章，品牌图片移至 `docs/assets`。\n- 公开 Release 继续仅提供五个平台的纯 Core 归档，每个归档包含 Core、`LICENSE` 和 `source.json`。Compose 镜像使用 `ghcr.io/alonabot/alonabot:0.1.1`，整合 WebUI 与 Agent；旧版本资产和 tag 保留。\n\n### Fixed\n\n- 媒体 URL 读取沿用当前授权与挂载路径，节点查询中的媒体登记到调用会话，供后续读取。\n- Core 日志 API 返回正式版本内容，按 `Accept-Language` 选择英文或简体中文，缺省或未匹配时回退英文，使更新界面可以显示对应版本的发行说明，并排除未发布变更。见 [PR #295](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/pull/295)。\n\n### 升级与兼容性\n\n升级前正常停止 Core 并备份完整数据目录，替换程序或更新固定版本的 Compose 镜像后，使用同一数据目录启动。安装记录、来源绑定、组件代次和 Adapter 实例配置继续保留。组件普通卸载保留数据与来源，可从同一来源重装。\n\n管理 CLI 使用 `--data-dir` 替代 `--token-file` 或 `ALONABOT_ADMIN_TOKEN`；远程 Core 通过 SSH 或 `docker exec` 操作。若旧版登录已删除 `admin_token`，停止 Core 后执行 `alonabot admin-token reset --data-dir <data_dir>` 恢复本机 CLI 访问；重置会撤销已有管理会话。\n\nOneBot 11 v0.1.1 可在 Core v0.1.0 启动；节点查询使用新增 Core 服务，旧版会返回 `Core service not found`，需要升级 Core。已有官方签名组件沿用其独立发行和验签安装流程，help 继续使用 v0.1.0。\n\n本版在 darwin/arm64 完成五目标交叉构建与归档静态检查，并通过 CLI、HTTP 管理端交叉安装、启用、卸载和同源重装公开签名组件。公开 OneBot 11 v0.1.1 与 help v0.1.0 在真实 QQ 测试群完成 `/help` 回复；Core 重启后再次回复，安装记录、Active 代次和实例配置保留。\n\n其余平台的实际运行覆盖与已批准延期沿用 [v0.1.0 发行记录](https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/blob/main/changelog/v0.1.0/zh-CN.md)；Windows 实际运行和 CGO 延期保持原决定。\n\n[0.1.1]: https://github.com/AlonaBot/AlonaBot/releases/tag/v0.1.1\n\n",
}
